Sidekick Codex plugin

Install:
  For a new installation, validate bundled skills and assemble the plugin with current Archify and PPT Master resources.
  For an existing installation, preserve plugin files; use wsley upgrade sidekick to synchronize skill and tool resources.
  Prepare and verify managed environments, register the Wsley local marketplace, enable Sidekick and apply managed Codex settings.

Upgrade:
  Skip the operation when Sidekick is not installed.
  Assemble bundled skills and current upstream tool resources, synchronize dependencies and verify environments before replacing changed plugin files and caches.
  Repair marketplace registration, enable Sidekick and apply managed Codex settings.

Status:
  Report plugin registration, tool source records, Codex settings, runtime package versions, Chromium binding, presentation dependencies and system packages.
  Use bounded local diagnostics without modifying configuration, installing dependencies or querying external services; omit the live browser launch test.

Requirements:
  Ubuntu, APT, AWK and a regular user with sudo access.
  An installed Codex CLI with plugin marketplace commands and marketplace-filtered listings through --marketplace.
  Preflight validates the local platform, commands, paths and CLI capabilities.
  Installation and upgrades require access to the relevant GitHub, npm, Python, Chromium and APT sources.
  The uv installation command must support JSON dry-run plans through --dry-run --output-format json.

Configuration:
  Marketplace root: ${XDG_DATA_HOME:-$HOME/.local/share}/sidekick
  Plugin source: ${XDG_DATA_HOME:-$HOME/.local/share}/sidekick/plugin
  Plugin registration: sidekick@wsley; installed plugin files are managed by the Codex plugin cache.
  Codex configuration: ${CODEX_HOME:-$HOME/.codex}/config.toml
  Managed environments: ${XDG_DATA_HOME:-$HOME/.local/share}/sidekick/runtimes

  Plugin listings select the wsley marketplace; plugin and marketplace list queries have a 15-second timeout.
  Manage one <wsley-sidekick>...</wsley-sidekick> block in developer_instructions, preserving user text outside it and directing Mira to resume unfinished work after compaction or handoffs.
  Set agents.max_concurrent_threads_per_session to 20 spawned-agent threads, excluding the primary thread; preserve other settings, custom roles and TOML comments.
  Validate Codex configuration before preparing runtime environments and skip configuration writes when managed values already match.

  Entry skill: sidekick:mira; describe project work naturally, with task coordination and specialist routing maintained in the bundled skills.
  Local skills are maintained in assets/sidekick/skills and use the host's default automatic selection; assembly preserves these methods instead of replacing them with upstream instructions.
  Skills use the target project's contracts and supported versions; examples do not prescribe its domain model, layout or capabilities.
  Task materials with a concrete downstream consumer or requested delivery use <project>/.sidekick/<timestamp>-<task>/, organized by purpose and execution; reuse the task root across stages and recovery and remove materials when their consumers finish.
  Build products, command output, tool caches, environments, temporary files and registered runtime state retain their project or native ownership.
  Each skill has name and description frontmatter, agents/openai.yaml interface metadata and a LICENSE containing applicable terms and upstream references with full commit hashes.
  assets/upstream.json declares complete version-coupled resources under vendor/<name>, including original instructions, scripts, templates and licenses; local adapters preserve technical contracts while applying task scope and confirmed decisions.
  Acquire tool resources through project-scoped pnpx skills@latest with --copy, resolving each repository HEAD once unless revision and pin_reason declare a compatibility constraint.
  Record acquired commits and content hashes in skills-lock.json; upgrades resolve current sources rather than treating this record as a version pin.

  Resolve published browser and draw.io MCP package versions into runtime-packages.json and generate mcp.json with managed executable paths.
  Reuse runtime packages when recorded versions and executable entries match; back up existing package directories before installing a replacement.
  The browser CLI supplies version-matched instructions and installs Chromium with Linux dependencies; activation verifies the browser with an offline launch test.
  Bind Archify to runtimes/chromium with ARCHIFY_CHROME and ARCHIFY_UPDATE_CHECK_DISABLED=1, preserving an unchanged binding.
  Presentations use Python 3.12, vendor/ppt-master/requirements.txt and the system tools in components.tsv.
  Reuse a valid presentation environment; rebuild one that is missing, damaged or uses another Python version. Reject symlinked runtime directories and replace environment symlinks without following their targets.
  Resolve presentation dependency changes with a read-only uv plan; back up and update the environment only when changes are planned, resolving newer dependencies during upgrades.
  Wsley prepares these environments for direct skill use; project toolchains, dependencies, accounts, keys and remote services retain their project or task configuration.

  Back up existing targets before changes, preserving symlinks as links; publish Codex configuration and Chromium bindings by atomic replacement without modifying link targets.
  Preserve identical plugin sources and caches and reuse existing marketplace registration.
  Reuse a configuration snapshot while its contents, permissions and link state remain unchanged within an activation; save a separate snapshot for each subsequent changed state.
  Restore affected plugin files and configuration if activation fails. Assembly or environment validation failure leaves them untouched; completed dependency changes remain, and failures do not select older upstream resources.
  Browser downloads and Python interpreter caches follow their tools' storage settings; global skill directories are not modified.
  Open a new Codex conversation after installation or upgrade to load the plugin and entry instruction.
